{"subjectId":"javascript","id":"parameters","title":"Parameters, Defaults & Rest","group":"Functions & Scope","order":14,"html":"<p class=\"lead\">JavaScript never checks argument counts: missing ones are <code>undefined</code>, extras are ignored — defaults, rest parameters and destructuring make that manageable.</p>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-question-mark\"></i>Missing and extra arguments</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>function show(a, b) {\n  console.log(a, b, arguments.length);\n}\nshow(1);\nshow(1, 2, 3);</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>1 undefined 1\n1 2 3</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-adjustments-horizontal\"></i>Default parameters</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>function greet(name = \"guest\", greeting = `Hello, ${name}`) {\n  return greeting;\n}\nconsole.log(greet());\nconsole.log(greet(\"Asha\"));\nconsole.log(greet(undefined, \"Hey\"));   // undefined triggers the default\nconsole.log(greet(null));               // null does not</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>Hello, guest\nHello, Asha\nHey\nHello, null</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"callout callout--note\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Key point</div><p>Defaults are evaluated <strong>at call time</strong>, left to right, and can refer to earlier parameters. A fresh <code>[]</code> default is created on every call — no Python-style shared mutable default.</p></div>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>function append(item, list = []) {\n  list.push(item);\n  return list;\n}\nconsole.log(append(1), append(2));\nlet counter = 0;\nconst next = (id = ++counter) =&gt; id;\nconsole.log(next(), next(), next(99), next());</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>[ 1 ] [ 2 ]\n1 2 99 3</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-dots\"></i>Rest parameters vs <code>arguments</code></h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>function oldStyle() {\n  console.log(Array.isArray(arguments), Array.from(arguments));\n}\nfunction modern(first, ...rest) {\n  console.log(first, rest, Array.isArray(rest));\n}\noldStyle(1, 2);\nmodern(1, 2, 3);\nmodern(1);</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>false [ 1, 2 ]\n1 [ 2, 3 ] true\n1 [] true</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th></th><th><code>arguments</code></th><th><code>...rest</code></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Type</td><td>Array-like object (no <code>map</code>)</td><td>Real array</td></tr><tr><td>In arrow functions</td><td>Not available</td><td>Works</td></tr><tr><td>Contains</td><td>All arguments</td><td>Only the <em>remaining</em> ones</td></tr><tr><td>Position</td><td>—</td><td>Must be the last parameter</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-list-details\"></i>Named options via destructuring</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>function createUser({ name, role = \"viewer\", active = true } = {}) {\n  return `${name} (${role}${active ? \"\" : \", inactive\"})`;\n}\nconsole.log(createUser({ name: \"Ravi\" }));\nconsole.log(createUser({ name: \"Mei\", role: \"admin\", active: false }));\nconsole.log(createUser());</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>Ravi (viewer)\nMei (admin, inactive)\nundefined (viewer)</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"callout callout--good\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Do</div><p>Use an options object for functions with more than 2–3 parameters: call sites become self-documenting and argument order stops mattering.</p></div>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>What is the arguments object?</summary><div><p>An array-like object available inside regular (non-arrow) functions holding every argument passed. It has <code>length</code> and indices but no array methods. Prefer rest parameters in modern code.</p></div></details></section>"}